Store the size of a ``NamedBlobFile`` and the dimensions of a ``NamedBlobImage`` when the data is written.
Before, ``getSize()`` read the size from the blob after every cache miss, which on remote blob storages means downloading the whole file.
``getImageSize()`` read the whole blob and wrote to the database on every call for images with unknown dimensions.
Opening a ``NamedBlobFile`` for writing now also drops a persisted size.
[jensens]
